rationale:
`assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with front matter, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions`.

Its `description` says when to use the skill in terms of the user's task. It applies:
- during design sessions;
- before changing code, tests, or requirement text in a Habeas-tracked project;
- even when the user only asks for a feature, bug fix, CLI flag, test, dependency bump, or wording tweak;
- when writing or revising reference chapters.

The description also names other bundled skills to use instead where an agent could confuse them. It points to `habeas-refactor` for moving code or requirements and to `habeas-evidence` for validation findings. Both exist under `assets/skills`. The requirement permits this with MAY, so it is not a gap.

The description does more than summarize the skill's workflow. The workflow part ("Drafts or edits requirements… implements and adds references") is extra material alongside the trigger conditions, and the requirement doesn't forbid it. The site meets the one MUST, and there are no violation matches to judge.
